{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": "The kinds of process Mac Analyzers tells apart, and how each is recognised. Read by the app and by agent-runner (AnalyzersKit/Memory/Kinds); the guard script does not read it. A process belongs to the category the census put it in (apps, tools, system); the kind says what it is inside that category. Recognition is by identity where the system gives one: bundle identifier, executable, program path, launchd job. A rule that can only go by a name says so (basis name) and its kind says why (nameOnlyBecause). Order matters: within a pass the first kind that matches wins. Pass 1 is the identity rules, pass 2 the name rules, pass 3 the kinds marked generic, then the category's fallback kind. Kind names are in Names.swift (Names.Kind), not here.",
